+USE-PACKAGE,symbols and namespaces,dialect_gap,names / sys\name / import / ordinary graph paths; explicit symbol provider only for CL compatibility,"LMX names and imports solve ordinary naming, but CL interned-symbol identity, package tables and symbol value/function/plist cells are not claimed. See TZ gap L02.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+USE-VALUE,resumable conditions,dialect_gap,ordinary callbacks / explicit continuation protocols / throw-catch-finally,Named nonlocal exits are available. Stack-resuming CL restarts and non-unwinding handler search require an explicit contract/provider if that exact feature is requested; no fake restart wrapper. L05.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+USER-HOMEDIR-PATHNAME,filesystem and paths,provider_gap,ordinary host/provider functions through the C/host boundary,"Path parsing, OS effects, filesystem metadata and CL logical-pathname translations require a concrete host profile. This archive supplies no fabricated filesystem implementation. L07.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+VALUES,multiple values and destructuring,native_composition,ordinary structured return / positional destructuring / explicit copy field stream / apply,LMX returns one ordinary value whose fields represent results; explicit consumers select/unpack it. This solves the task without pretending CL multiple-value arity/truncation semantics exist implicitly. L01.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+VALUES-LIST,multiple values and destructuring,native_composition,ordinary structured return / positional destructuring / explicit copy field stream / apply,LMX returns one ordinary value whose fields represent results; explicit consumers select/unpack it. This solves the task without pretending CL multiple-value arity/truncation semantics exist implicitly. L01.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+VARIABLE,environment variables and markers,profile_or_metadata,ordinary explicit/dynamic owner fields and selected host profile,A CL dynamic configuration variable or REPL/history marker is not an LMX function; task-specific policy can be an ordinary owner field. Exact CL global state is not emulated.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+VECTOR,arrays and storage,native_with_gap,T[] / ordinary indexing / length / resize / reserve / slice / append / insertAt / deleteAt,"LMX Arrays have an existing typed storage/capacity contract. CL displaced arrays, fill-pointer behavior and exact rank/layout reflection are not silently aliases of one-dimensional sequence helpers.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+VECTOR-POP,arrays and storage,native_with_gap,T[] / ordinary indexing / length / resize / reserve / slice / append / insertAt / deleteAt,"LMX Arrays have an existing typed storage/capacity contract. CL displaced arrays, fill-pointer behavior and exact rank/layout reflection are not silently aliases of one-dimensional sequence helpers.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+VECTOR-PUSH,arrays and storage,native_with_gap,T[] / ordinary indexing / length / resize / reserve / slice / append / insertAt / deleteAt,"LMX Arrays have an existing typed storage/capacity contract. CL displaced arrays, fill-pointer behavior and exact rank/layout reflection are not silently aliases of one-dimensional sequence helpers.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+VECTOR-PUSH-EXTEND,arrays and storage,native_with_gap,T[] / ordinary indexing / length / resize / reserve / slice / append / insertAt / deleteAt,"LMX Arrays have an existing typed storage/capacity contract. CL displaced arrays, fill-pointer behavior and exact rank/layout reflection are not silently aliases of one-dimensional sequence helpers.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+VECTORP,arrays and storage,native_with_gap,T[] / ordinary indexing / length / resize / reserve / slice / append / insertAt / deleteAt,"LMX Arrays have an existing typed storage/capacity contract. CL displaced arrays, fill-pointer behavior and exact rank/layout reflection are not silently aliases of one-dimensional sequence helpers.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WARN,conditions and diagnostics,native_with_gap,throws / throw / catch / sys\assert / ordinary typed payload,Concrete named failures map directly on the stated task. CL condition inheritance and restart behavior do not follow from this mapping.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WARNING,conditions and diagnostics,native_with_gap,throws / throw / catch / sys\assert / ordinary typed payload,Concrete named failures map directly on the stated task. CL condition inheritance and restart behavior do not follow from this mapping.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WHEN,control binding and places,native_or_composition,if / else / while / break / return / := / compound assignment / throw-catch-finally / ordinary dynamic binding,"Use the existing receiver/Expression and typed place contract. CL generalized SETF macros, catch tag identity and restarts need their exact task qualification; no lexical-visibility restriction is added to dynamic names.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WILD-PATHNAME-P,filesystem and paths,provider_gap,ordinary host/provider functions through the C/host boundary,"Path parsing, OS effects, filesystem metadata and CL logical-pathname translations require a concrete host profile. This archive supplies no fabricated filesystem implementation. L07.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WITH-ACCESSORS,CLOS and object protocol,native_with_gap,ordinary Structure methods / full structural requirements / copy / merge / graph-field access,"Ordinary object tasks use native Structures. Full CLOS multiple dispatch, method combination, class redefinition and the MOP are not equated with a single LMX method call. L04.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WITH-COMPILATION-UNIT,compilation and system construction,profile_or_metadata,ordinary source/native profiles / explicit compilation / import / build tooling,Compiler policy and load-time phases belong to the implementation/toolchain; no automatic recompilation or foreign ABI reuse is introduced as a source shortcut. L13.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WITH-CONDITION-RESTARTS,conditions and diagnostics,native_with_gap,throws / throw / catch / sys\assert / ordinary typed payload,Concrete named failures map directly on the stated task. CL condition inheritance and restart behavior do not follow from this mapping.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WITH-HASH-TABLE-ITERATOR,hash tables,provider_or_library_gap,assoc / explicit same callback / memoize; hash provider when complexity is required,"Linear association/memo lookup covers finite tasks without pretending O(1) hashing. General hashing consistent with equality, weak keys, mutation and identity needs its own contract. L09.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WITH-INPUT-FROM-STRING,streams and I/O,provider_gap,ordinary text/resource state and finally / bracket / host I/O profile,Control scaffolding is reusable; exact CL stream/syntax state still needs a provider. No claim that a string Array alone implements every stream operation. L07.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WITH-OPEN-FILE,streams and I/O,provider_gap,ordinary text/resource state and finally / bracket / host I/O profile,Control scaffolding is reusable; exact CL stream/syntax state still needs a provider. No claim that a string Array alone implements every stream operation. L07.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WITH-OPEN-STREAM,streams and I/O,provider_gap,ordinary resource values / finally or bracket / host I/O provider,"Resource control is available; actual stream I/O, buffering, encoding, interactive behavior and Gray-style extension need provider contracts. L07.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WITH-OUTPUT-TO-STRING,streams and I/O,provider_gap,ordinary text/resource state and finally / bracket / host I/O profile,Control scaffolding is reusable; exact CL stream/syntax state still needs a provider. No claim that a string Array alone implements every stream operation. L07.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WITH-PACKAGE-ITERATOR,symbols and namespaces,dialect_gap,names / sys\name / import / ordinary graph paths; explicit symbol provider only for CL compatibility,"LMX names and imports solve ordinary naming, but CL interned-symbol identity, package tables and symbol value/function/plist cells are not claimed. See TZ gap L02.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WITH-SIMPLE-RESTART,resumable conditions,dialect_gap,ordinary callbacks / explicit continuation protocols / throw-catch-finally,Named nonlocal exits are available. Stack-resuming CL restarts and non-unwinding handler search require an explicit contract/provider if that exact feature is requested; no fake restart wrapper. L05.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WITH-SLOTS,CLOS and object protocol,native_with_gap,ordinary Structure methods / full structural requirements / copy / merge / graph-field access,"Ordinary object tasks use native Structures. Full CLOS multiple dispatch, method combination, class redefinition and the MOP are not equated with a single LMX method call. L04.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WITH-STANDARD-IO-SYNTAX,streams and I/O,provider_gap,ordinary text/resource state and finally / bracket / host I/O profile,Control scaffolding is reusable; exact CL stream/syntax state still needs a provider. No claim that a string Array alone implements every stream operation. L07.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WRITE,printing and FORMAT,provider_or_library_gap,toLmx / formatInt / limited positional format / explicit text operations,"These shorten serialization/display tasks, but full CL FORMAT directives, pretty-printer dispatch and readably round-tripping arbitrary Lisp objects are not implemented by positional format. L06.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WRITE-BYTE,streams and I/O,provider_gap,ordinary resource values / finally or bracket / host I/O provider,"Resource control is available; actual stream I/O, buffering, encoding, interactive behavior and Gray-style extension need provider contracts. L07.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WRITE-CHAR,streams and I/O,provider_gap,ordinary resource values / finally or bracket / host I/O provider,"Resource control is available; actual stream I/O, buffering, encoding, interactive behavior and Gray-style extension need provider contracts. L07.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WRITE-LINE,streams and I/O,provider_gap,ordinary resource values / finally or bracket / host I/O provider,"Resource control is available; actual stream I/O, buffering, encoding, interactive behavior and Gray-style extension need provider contracts. L07.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WRITE-SEQUENCE,streams and I/O,provider_gap,ordinary resource values / finally or bracket / host I/O provider,"Resource control is available; actual stream I/O, buffering, encoding, interactive behavior and Gray-style extension need provider contracts. L07.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WRITE-STRING,streams and I/O,provider_gap,ordinary resource values / finally or bracket / host I/O provider,"Resource control is available; actual stream I/O, buffering, encoding, interactive behavior and Gray-style extension need provider contracts. L07.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+WRITE-TO-STRING,printing and FORMAT,provider_or_library_gap,toLmx / formatInt / limited positional format / explicit text operations,"These shorten serialization/display tasks, but full CL FORMAT directives, pretty-printer dispatch and readably round-tripping arbitrary Lisp objects are not implemented by positional format. L06.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+Y-OR-N-P,interactive tools and debugging,profile_or_metadata,LMX observation/debugging contract and explicit host tooling,Interactive UI/debugger facilities are not algorithmic aliases. Runtime state inspection and stepping need real executor support; no transcript or inferred state is presented as execution. L13.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+YES-OR-NO-P,interactive tools and debugging,profile_or_metadata,LMX observation/debugging contract and explicit host tooling,Interactive UI/debugger facilities are not algorithmic aliases. Runtime state inspection and stepping need real executor support; no transcript or inferred state is presented as execution. L13.,NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
+ZEROP,scalar arithmetic,native_or_composition,ordinary + - * / != < <= = > >= ** % and explicit numeric context,"Use the native operation on the agreed numeric domain. CL MOD vs REM signs, division exactness, unary/variadic arity and overflow profiles must match; they are not silently identical.",NOT_RUN,https://www.lispworks.com/documentation/HyperSpec/Body/01_i.htm,../../../LMX_semantics.en.md
